<p>President Donald Trump used a prime-time White House address on 2026-04-02 to say the United States would complete its objectives in the conflict with Iran &quot;shortly&quot; and would hit Iran &quot;extremely hard&quot; over the next two to three weeks. Multiple outlets said the speech came after more than a month of fighting that, according to Politico and the Financial Times, began with a White House-launched joint operation against Tehran in February. Coverage across outlets met the new timeline with broad skepticism because Trump has repeatedly used similar two-week or two-to-three-week windows on other major issues, including the Russia-Ukraine war, without producing a settlement. The uncertainty grew after a senior Iranian leader answered the address defiantly, while US intelligence reporting cited by NDTV said Iran still retains missile and drone capacity — a sign the fighting may continue even as Washington says it is nearing its goals.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vlOMQyupCJSBnreXYKJHNyAdF2ImdgzmaoB5gblb7f-Lq_sDDG7fDgJUltLw4nuLz8pAm_Xg2qUEpQBJyGb0XnBnnnhQaWR8x5NlRR__JTTGa8jiaP6YNOxQWtfM5ke-xytXGltsMYaZ-LK3X62iLffPXlrAHa74d4QtLReAL3r27Q_Qu_kH3JEYCKuq-zFEhvkwLQ7QyN1RhukYf1dBSws8cafoop5cq6E' alt='Workers inspecting the damage from a strike by Iran on Petah Tikva, Israel, on Thursday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Public skepticism: PBS reported that Trump was asking an increasingly skeptical electorate for more time as American tolerance for the conflict kept wearing thin.</li><li>Negotiating strain: The Financial Times said Trump&#x27;s dealmaking approach has left him with few good options to end a war that, in its account, he started more than a month ago.</li><li>Deadline risk: The New York Times said Trump could reach the end of his own two-to-three-week window with little changed on the ground, increasing pressure on the White House to explain what comes next.</li></ul><blockquote>We are on track to complete all of America’s military objectives shortly, very shortly. We’re going to hit them extremely hard over the next two to three weeks. - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>President Donald Trump: AllSides portrayed the address as a full-throated defense of the war, highlighting how aggressively the White House had to make its case to Americans at home. (<a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-02-0700/donald-trump-trump-makes-his-best-case-war-fails-ease-worries-about-how-it-will-end'>AllSides</a>)</li><li>Financial Times analysis: The paper argued that Trump&#x27;s dealmaking playbook has left him with few good options to end the war, despite his effort to project control in the White House address. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/0f9f2038-7274-4d73-b55e-d8d2f88ee951'>Financial Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.politico.com/news/2026/04/02/trump-two-three-weeks-iran-timeline-00856287'>Why Trump’s ‘2 to 3 week’ timeline for ending Iran war sounds familiar</a> - politico.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/videos/ce8jz0239jxo'>Watch: Trump&#x27;s shifting deadlines for ending Iran war</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.allsides.com/news/2026-04-02-0700/donald-trump-trump-makes-his-best-case-war-fails-ease-worries-about-how-it-will-end'>Trump makes his best case for the war — but fails to ease worries about how it will end</a> - allsides.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/0f9f2038-7274-4d73-b55e-d8d2f88ee951'>The art of the deal eludes Trump in Iran</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/politics/with-iran-war-address-trump-urges-increasingly-skeptical-electorate-to-give-him-a-bit-more-time'>With Iran war address, Trump urges increasingly skeptical electorate to give him a bit more time</a> - pbs.org</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/02/world/middleeast/iran-war-middle-east-recap-thursday.html'>Here’s What Happened in the War in the Middle East on Thursday<